WEBVTT

00:00.000 --> 00:03.020
Shinjuku Police Station

00:02.500 --> 00:03.520
The Gator Sisters.

00:03.020 --> 00:04.040
<b><Gator Sisters></b>

00:04.160 --> 00:05.620
<b><Barber></b>

00:04.290 --> 00:05.620
The Barber.

00:05.620 --> 00:07.080
<b><Riddle Riddle></b>

00:05.840 --> 00:07.080
Riddle Riddle.

00:07.170 --> 00:08.670
<b><Grocer></b>

00:07.410 --> 00:08.670
The Grocer.

00:08.670 --> 00:10.090
<b><Poisoner></b>

00:08.860 --> 00:10.090
The Poisoner.

00:10.170 --> 00:11.630
<b><Donner Donner></b>

00:10.330 --> 00:11.630
Donner Donner.

00:11.630 --> 00:14.740
<b><Phantom Solitaire></b>

00:11.630 --> 00:14.740
And Phantom Solitaire.

00:14.740 --> 00:19.370
<b><i>Troublemakers     Troublemakers at Large</i></b>

00:14.740 --> 00:19.370
As you know, everyone on this 
list is now in custody or dead.

00:19.370 --> 00:22.130
Who gave them those weird nicknames?

00:22.130 --> 00:23.300
He did.

00:23.300 --> 00:25.750
You there! Cut the chitchat!

00:26.000 --> 00:29.570
What's wrong with nicknames?
Not like they'll ever go public.

00:29.570 --> 00:31.360
<i>Sounds like </i>someone's<i> self-conscious.</i>

00:31.360 --> 00:32.170
Anyway!

00:32.170 --> 00:38.760
<b><i>Troublemakers</i></b>

00:32.490 --> 00:38.760
Cracking cases we can't make public, 
and that no one would believe if we did,

00:39.100 --> 00:43.760
is our job here at Materials Compiling 
Group #3, or Comps-3 for short.

00:44.210 --> 00:45.230
Now...

00:45.460 --> 00:46.460
<b><Grim Reaper></b>

00:45.570 --> 00:46.460
the Grim Reaper,

00:46.460 --> 00:47.730
<b><Fire-Breathing Bug></b>

00:46.900 --> 00:48.150
the Fire-Breathing Bug,

00:47.730 --> 00:49.900
<b><Lemmings></b>

00:48.150 --> 00:49.900
and Lemmings.

00:50.380 --> 00:53.490
These three troublemakers are still at large.

00:53.490 --> 00:56.740
Add to that the skeletons 
in the fire two days ago

00:56.740 --> 00:59.660
and the human knots yesterday.

00:59.660 --> 01:05.080
Also, one set of footprints at the scene 
of the human knots matched Lemmings's.

01:05.080 --> 01:15.300
<b><i>Troublemakers     Troublemakers at Large</i></b>

01:07.030 --> 01:12.110
And we think the Fire-Breathing Bug started 
the fire the skeletons appeared in.

01:12.110 --> 01:15.290
We don't know if they're connected 
to the human knots yet,

01:15.680 --> 01:20.790
but evidence points to two troublemakers 
in a couple of days. We can't ignore that.

01:20.790 --> 01:22.950
Could the skeletons be CGI?

01:22.950 --> 01:27.370
Their size and perspective is 
consistent across multiple videos.

01:27.370 --> 01:32.770
If that was faked in real time, 
all video evidence would be worthless.

01:33.200 --> 01:34.030
End of story.

01:34.280 --> 01:38.340
And if they were smoke and mirrors, 
how did the kids get out?

01:38.340 --> 01:41.860
Social media and occult websites 
can't stop talking about it.

01:41.330 --> 01:47.250
<b><i>Troublemakers</i></b>

01:42.280 --> 01:43.890
Well, don't panic.

01:44.210 --> 01:47.250
We managed to explain all 
the others in the end.

01:47.780 --> 01:52.710
Even Phantom Solitaire turned out 
to just be an incredibly skilled person.

01:53.220 --> 01:59.470
None of our cases have turned up a real 
ghost or dragon-summoning wizard.

01:59.960 --> 02:03.820
And that won't change. 
The perp is always human.

02:05.420 --> 02:07.560
And, since they're human,

02:08.090 --> 02:10.020
we can take them.

03:51.220 --> 03:53.080
There. It worked.

03:53.390 --> 03:57.710
I moved Polka-kun's original 
soul into this stuffed animal,

03:57.710 --> 03:59.690
so you can have your drone back.

03:59.690 --> 04:02.760
Oh! Welcome home, my darling drone-chan!

04:03.180 --> 04:06.180
How I've missed you!

04:06.510 --> 04:10.390
Really, I ought to call <i>you</i> Polka-kun,

04:10.800 --> 04:14.140
but I'll be borrowing your name
and identity a little longer. Sorry.

04:14.140 --> 04:15.870
I promise I'll make it up to you.

04:18.110 --> 04:19.070
Oh!

04:19.070 --> 04:21.190
What's this?! It's so cute!

04:21.190 --> 04:23.210
Did you buy it, Polka-kun?

04:23.950 --> 04:26.100
Wow! It turned red!

04:26.100 --> 04:29.280
<i>He gets turned on by the girl who killed him?</i>

04:29.700 --> 04:32.200
I guess the real Polka was a weirdo, too.

04:33.790 --> 04:35.530
I can't tell what he's trying to say.

04:35.870 --> 04:37.750
I could make it so he can talk.

04:37.750 --> 04:38.500
Huh?

04:38.850 --> 04:41.490
I'd only need fresh human vocal cords.

04:41.490 --> 04:43.130
Those ain't easy to get!

04:43.450 --> 04:47.080
Creating them from nothing 
would drain a lot of mana.

04:47.080 --> 04:51.100
I suppose I ought to replenish my 
magical power before I focus on money.

04:51.470 --> 04:57.420
But this world has so little mana in 
the air, and I sense so few spirits.

04:57.420 --> 04:58.440
So, what'll you do?

04:58.880 --> 05:01.960
I can usually draw on ghosts for power.

05:01.960 --> 05:07.060
It takes more energy than you'd think to 
keep a human soul in the living world.

05:07.430 --> 05:09.420
Grudges, regrets, that sort of thing.

05:10.580 --> 05:17.840
And by exorcising ghosts, necromancers 
can convert that power into magic.

05:18.840 --> 05:23.800
That made this building an even better 
source of mana than an old battlefield.

05:24.090 --> 05:27.560
You won't find many other 
places like this, you know?

05:27.560 --> 05:28.770
Don't worry!

05:29.220 --> 05:32.010
Your world has mana stones, 
just like mine did!

05:32.010 --> 05:33.380
Mana-what-now?

05:33.580 --> 05:36.230
<b><i>Gemstones of the World</i></b>

05:33.760 --> 05:36.230
They're rocks. You call them "gemstones" here.

05:36.230 --> 05:41.700
Diamonds, sapphires, and the like were 
high-density mana stones in my world.

05:42.750 --> 05:45.760
With just one bucket of them,

05:45.760 --> 05:50.680
I'll have all the arcane power I need 
to strike it rich in this world.

05:52.090 --> 05:53.700
Wow. Amazing.

05:54.780 --> 05:57.330
Now, go take a look at reality.

05:58.420 --> 05:59.630
Pardon?

06:01.130 --> 06:08.090
Th-This one stone costs thirty times 
one of your officials' daily wages?

06:08.450 --> 06:10.930
I never dreamed it would be so costly.

06:10.930 --> 06:13.720
Were they cheaper in your world?

06:13.720 --> 06:16.910
Yes, even children could easily afford them.

06:14.520 --> 06:17.590
<b>The Imperial Dazzling Corps 
keeps the peace!</b>

06:14.520 --> 06:18.230
<b>Everyday convenience thanks to magical circuitry!</b>

06:16.500 --> 06:18.230
<b>Heaps of mana stones from magic-rich caves!</b>

06:16.910 --> 06:18.230
Wow.

06:19.550 --> 06:22.970
But for the sake of a peaceful life,
 I'll persevere.

06:23.290 --> 06:28.490
If I save up enough money to buy every 
jewel in this shop, I can manage.

06:28.010 --> 06:29.820
<b>Putting the cart before the horse</b>

06:29.820 --> 06:36.870
At this afternoon's market values, 
that would be 3,812,795,800 yen.

06:37.270 --> 06:40.970
I'm not used to this currency, 
so that doesn't quite click.

06:42.660 --> 06:44.380
Thank you very much.

06:45.770 --> 06:48.510
And I could feel such potent 
mana from the stones...

06:48.890 --> 06:51.910
Can't you suck out the 
magic through the cases?

06:51.910 --> 06:54.510
The stones would crumble if I did.

06:54.840 --> 06:57.310
That wouldn't be fair to the shopkeepers.

06:57.310 --> 06:59.610
<i>So, you've got scruples about theft?</i>

07:00.310 --> 07:03.270
<i>Okay. Now what?</i>

07:03.270 --> 07:04.190
<i>Hm?</i>

07:07.370 --> 07:08.110
Crap!

07:13.500 --> 07:14.950
Don't be so cold.

07:15.260 --> 07:17.170
What are you running for,

07:17.660 --> 07:19.410
criminal?

07:19.620 --> 07:23.540
Hey. Glad I managed to catch 
you today, Clarissa-chan.

07:23.540 --> 07:25.880
What brings you here, Inspector?

07:25.880 --> 07:30.170
Oh, I've been dying to chat with you.

07:30.450 --> 07:36.250
Your people were awfully busy when the 
Shakuzawa Building caught fire, yeah?

07:37.310 --> 07:41.660
That info broker's drones 
were spotted near the scene.

07:41.660 --> 07:45.520
Then, yesterday, we found 
some guys in real bad shape.

07:45.520 --> 07:49.990
They worked for one of your 
lackeys, a guy called Jinba.

07:50.710 --> 07:54.160
It got me wondering if there's a connection.

07:54.960 --> 07:59.070
So, being a cop, I'm gonna need 
to ask you some questions.

08:02.170 --> 08:05.630
How deep is your organization 
mixed up in this,

08:06.020 --> 08:07.460
Lisa Kuraki?

08:11.620 --> 08:15.320
Oh, sorry. Did I startle you?

08:15.320 --> 08:16.890
Don't mind me.

08:16.890 --> 08:18.290
Please.

08:18.620 --> 08:19.970
O-Okay.

08:19.970 --> 08:24.910
Watch out, Polka-kun. 
This guy's probably bad news.

08:24.910 --> 08:27.980
I know you can hear me, Takumi Kuruya-kun.

08:28.240 --> 08:32.950
You can talk through your drones when 
their propellers aren't spinning.

08:33.270 --> 08:36.740
<i>Of all the guys who could've 
caught me! What'll I do?!</i>

08:37.240 --> 08:40.720
<i>If he's not after Polka and Misaki, 
maybe I can play dumb?</i>

08:41.320 --> 08:42.160
Excuse me.

08:43.640 --> 08:48.670
I believe I asked you nicely to ignore me.

08:48.670 --> 08:53.920
You did, but that drone means 
a lot to a friend of mine.

08:54.500 --> 08:57.760
A friend? You mean Takumi-kun?

08:58.130 --> 08:58.900
Yes.

09:00.330 --> 09:05.080
That's no good. I mean, 
you must still be in high school.

09:05.080 --> 09:09.900
Hang around human garbage like him, 
and you'll end up just as rotten.

09:10.420 --> 09:14.110
Cut ties with him. Right here, right now.

09:14.840 --> 09:15.820
<i>What?</i>

09:16.130 --> 09:17.680
<i>He's awfully chilly.</i>

09:18.640 --> 09:22.910
Garbage? Scum? Impure?

09:24.060 --> 09:27.160
I think society decides 
who those labels apply to.

09:28.090 --> 09:28.920
But...

09:29.330 --> 09:32.870
<i>I</i> decide who my friends are.

09:40.060 --> 09:41.100
I see.

09:41.880 --> 09:43.560
Now I'm curious.

09:43.860 --> 09:49.020
Would you mind telling 
me a bit about yourself?

09:53.540 --> 09:55.100
<i>Kouzaburou Arase.</i>

09:55.730 --> 09:59.690
<i>He may be a detective with the 
Shinjuku Community Safety Division,</i>

09:59.690 --> 10:02.620
<i>but he's way scarier than any thug.</i>

10:03.720 --> 10:07.260
<i>When I used to run intel for 
a street gang, I saw him...</i>

10:09.770 --> 10:15.290
<i>demolish eight of their toughest 
fighters in no time flat.</i>

10:17.050 --> 10:18.110
<i>Can you hear me, Polka?</i>

10:18.110 --> 10:20.490
<i>Don't answer; he'll catch on.</i>

10:20.840 --> 10:22.510
Hide your power.

10:22.510 --> 10:25.270
If you catch his eye, 
you can kiss a peaceful life goodbye.

10:25.690 --> 10:27.180
<i>He's a cop.</i>

10:28.110 --> 10:30.400
Is he the one who asked you?

10:30.660 --> 10:32.300
To be friends, that is.

10:32.730 --> 10:36.510
You shouldn't trust strangers 
who act too friendly.

10:36.510 --> 10:38.860
Didn't your parents teach you that?

10:39.090 --> 10:42.030
My parents sold me, so I wouldn't know.

10:42.330 --> 10:43.780
They "sold" you?

10:44.630 --> 10:47.950
<i>Oh, sorry. That was in my past life.</i>

10:48.260 --> 10:50.250
Curiouser and curiouser.

10:50.250 --> 10:52.880
I'd really like to know your name.

10:53.970 --> 10:57.020
<i>Misaki visits Clarissa's too often.</i>

10:57.020 --> 11:00.090
<i>Polka probably will, too.
We can't afford an investigation!</i>

11:05.690 --> 11:07.560
<i>Hey, Arase, man.</i>

11:07.930 --> 11:10.270
It's been a while since our last chat.

11:10.270 --> 11:14.980
Now this is a surprise. 
You know my phone number?

11:14.980 --> 11:18.440
You must have really improved since then.

11:18.810 --> 11:23.480
Those are just my gaming buddies. 
Their relatives work at Clarissa's bar.

11:23.870 --> 11:27.610
They're not in on any shady stuff. 
Can't you cut 'em a break?

11:27.610 --> 11:31.370
I'm questioning them to find that out.

11:31.620 --> 11:35.660
Look, I know I'll get 
fined for illegal flying,

11:37.210 --> 11:41.980
but you'll get it worse if video of you 
hassling innocent kids hits the net.

11:42.620 --> 11:46.390
Really? You're trying to negotiate with <i>me</i>?

11:48.650 --> 11:52.270
Having some distance between 
us sure makes you cocky.

11:53.480 --> 11:56.670
Hard to believe you sold 
out your old buddies,

11:57.210 --> 12:01.940
wailing, "I'll tell you 
everything! Just don't hit me!"

12:02.650 --> 12:07.260
Hey, do you know what kind of 
guy Takumi Kuruya <i>really</i> is?

12:07.260 --> 12:11.460
He'd sell out his friends in a 
heartbeat to save his own skin.

12:11.730 --> 12:16.330
He told me how many moles their 
kid sisters have, and I didn't even ask.

12:16.330 --> 12:18.420
<i>How the hell would I know that?!</i>

12:18.690 --> 12:21.170
<i>He's a callous criminal.</i>

12:21.170 --> 12:24.130
<i>Who knows what he says about you 
behind your backs?</i>

12:24.130 --> 12:28.850
And he'll sell your secrets 
if you give him half a chance.

12:29.670 --> 12:31.320
<i>So he's loose-lipped?</i>

12:32.310 --> 12:36.090
But that's better than 
what you are right now.

12:37.600 --> 12:40.910
<i>I knew it. He's not just any kid.</i>

12:41.320 --> 12:44.670
<i>He's got the aura of a mob enforcer.</i>

12:44.670 --> 12:48.370
<i>Or maybe more like a 
battle-hardened boss.</i>

12:48.370 --> 12:51.450
<i>A veteran soldier? No, he couldn't be.</i>

12:52.150 --> 12:56.170
<i>I don't want him to see my 
power or figure out who I am.</i>

12:56.720 --> 12:59.540
<i>What will Misaki-chan do?</i>

12:59.940 --> 13:00.670
Huh?

13:02.010 --> 13:04.590
<i>Where'd the girl go?</i>

13:12.110 --> 13:13.950
Oh, I'm <i>so</i> scared!

13:13.950 --> 13:18.390
I just defended myself against a creep
 who was about to hit me, right?

13:15.500 --> 13:16.830
<b>Creep</b>

13:21.120 --> 13:22.860
Now, let's get out of here!

13:22.860 --> 13:25.070
He'll attack us if we stick around!

13:33.420 --> 13:36.370
No normal kid has a kick that strong.

13:41.580 --> 13:43.380
Where'd they go?

13:43.670 --> 13:45.130
That was close.

13:45.130 --> 13:46.720
To be honest, I owe you one.

13:46.720 --> 13:52.010
Kurupon texted me. It was all,
 "He's a cop. Run."

14:03.240 --> 14:05.160
<i>You okay, Polka?</i>

14:05.160 --> 14:07.030
Yeah, somehow.

14:07.840 --> 14:08.780
<i>Listen.</i>

14:09.300 --> 14:12.460
I appreciate you standing up for me,

14:12.990 --> 14:15.240
but you gave me too much credit back there.

14:16.890 --> 14:18.530
He was telling the truth.

14:18.880 --> 14:25.010
I don't wanna die, so I'll spill your 
secrets as soon as someone threatens me.

14:26.410 --> 14:28.290
<i>Now you're giving </i>me<i> too much credit.</i>

14:29.630 --> 14:34.150
I've got no secrets worth 
more than a friend's life.

14:37.950 --> 14:41.510
<i>Were you this hard-boiled 
in your past life, too?</i>

14:42.700 --> 14:45.530
I told you about the 
Geldwood Order, didn't I?

14:45.860 --> 14:50.130
Their holy arts can force people 
to confess against their will.

14:50.490 --> 14:54.630
So "selling me out" was an irrelevant concept.

14:54.630 --> 14:58.070
<i>Are you sure those guys were holy?</i>

15:00.390 --> 15:02.570
At least one of them was.

15:04.160 --> 15:06.180
Hi there, Aikawa-san.

15:06.550 --> 15:10.720
This may sound weird, but would 
you investigate this footprint?

15:11.610 --> 15:14.430
What the hell? That's wicked funny.

15:14.690 --> 15:17.970
Wait, that's a woman's shoe. 
The hell have you been doing?

15:17.970 --> 15:19.310
Arase-chan!

15:19.310 --> 15:22.270
<b>Shinjuku Precinct 
25-Year Veteran</b>

15:19.310 --> 15:22.270
<b>Fumiyo Yamada</b>

15:19.310 --> 15:22.270
m 0 0 l 140 0 140 70 0 70

15:19.310 --> 15:22.700
You're hurt! You need to 
get that treated first!

15:22.700 --> 15:24.640
Hurry! Get that shirt off!

15:24.640 --> 15:25.430
What? Hey!

15:25.430 --> 15:26.230
Hm?

15:25.700 --> 15:29.700
I've got it. Eh? It's not coming off...

15:26.230 --> 15:29.700
I don't think I'll even 
need to check this print.

15:29.700 --> 15:30.490
Come again?

15:30.490 --> 15:32.160
I mean, I just saw one.

15:32.780 --> 15:36.030
Apart from Lemmings's, 
it was the most important print

15:36.030 --> 15:38.760
at that human knot crime scene.

15:41.170 --> 15:42.500
Look at that.

15:42.910 --> 15:44.220
Scary, right?

15:44.220 --> 15:47.290
Anyway, if you're getting patched up,
 go somewhere private.

15:45.130 --> 15:49.650
I hear he got it while he 
was infiltrating the yakuza.

15:47.290 --> 15:49.650
That thing on your back freaks people out.

15:50.490 --> 15:51.630
Bingo.

15:51.630 --> 15:55.600
Finally, a case worth sinking my teeth into.

15:55.600 --> 15:58.380
This should be fun.

16:02.610 --> 16:05.740
Comps-3 sure is noisy.

16:05.740 --> 16:08.370
I hear they got a lead on Lemmings.

16:08.370 --> 16:10.320
What? That troublemaker?

16:10.940 --> 16:14.490
He first appeared five years ago,
 if I remember right.

16:15.000 --> 16:18.680
Murder, protection, 
transportation, kidnapping,

16:18.680 --> 16:22.330
robbery, destroying evidence, 
debt collection...

16:22.330 --> 16:26.210
Rumor has it he'll do any job.

16:28.050 --> 16:30.310
I saw him once myself.

16:31.130 --> 16:34.130
He was a monster all right.

16:34.570 --> 16:38.300
The guys he was fighting 
brought out submachine guns,

16:39.020 --> 16:41.100
but he still broke all their necks

16:41.100 --> 16:43.620
while they hosed him down with bullets.

16:44.480 --> 16:47.190
He didn't dodge. 
He did it while they shot him.

16:49.320 --> 16:52.900
I'd like to say we'll catch him ourselves,

16:53.210 --> 16:55.240
but that's Comps-3's jurisdiction.

16:55.760 --> 16:58.010
We've got to leave it to Iwanome's team.

16:59.240 --> 17:02.160
Iwanome's an oddball who 
lost his shot at promotion,

17:02.160 --> 17:05.930
but he's a lot tougher than he looks.

17:07.530 --> 17:09.540
So then I told 'im!

17:09.540 --> 17:12.760
"I've had it with your tricks!"

17:12.760 --> 17:13.840
Seriously?!

17:13.840 --> 17:16.020
That's something cannon fodder would say!

17:16.750 --> 17:19.840
What did that guy even come here for?

17:19.840 --> 17:21.970
To hear what we have to say.

17:22.190 --> 17:25.650
Informally, since he doesn't have a warrant.

17:25.650 --> 17:27.980
Hey, Lisa Kuraki!

17:28.520 --> 17:34.220
Fess up! I know you work with 
some serious troublemakers!

17:34.220 --> 17:35.650
C'mon!

17:35.650 --> 17:38.760
I don't mean Lemmings 
or the Fire-Breathing Bug!

17:38.760 --> 17:42.370
I know the Grim Reaper's one of your people!

17:42.370 --> 17:45.120
Who's that? They sound scary!

17:45.120 --> 17:48.330
Lemmings? What a cute name!

17:48.330 --> 17:53.020
Listen, there's nothing cute about Lemmings.

17:53.020 --> 17:58.370
He scared the hell out of me when 
he broke through a 30-man team.

17:58.370 --> 18:00.820
Oh, but don't tell the media that, okay?

18:00.820 --> 18:03.120
Hmm... I don't know.

18:03.120 --> 18:04.860
Should he be saying that?

18:04.860 --> 18:08.340
I thought the precinct 
couldn't make it public.

18:09.130 --> 18:11.580
No, but that doesn't matter.

18:11.580 --> 18:12.360
Huh?

18:12.360 --> 18:16.900
This bar is part of the underworld.

18:17.160 --> 18:20.450
Of course, I'm sure he's doing 
it on purpose to taunt us.

18:20.450 --> 18:26.140
Those skeletons walking through fire 
smell like a new troublemaker to me.

18:26.140 --> 18:28.220
What?! That's <i>so</i> creepy!

18:27.040 --> 18:28.990
We can't let him dig too deep.

18:28.990 --> 18:31.720
We'll need to warn Polka-kun 
to be careful later.

18:31.720 --> 18:33.710
Hiya, Clarissa!

18:33.710 --> 18:35.920
We're here to hang out!

18:36.230 --> 18:37.610
Why <i>now</i>?

18:38.580 --> 18:41.870
Whoa, there! You kids must be underage.

18:41.870 --> 18:44.160
You shouldn't be in here.

18:44.160 --> 18:46.560
Don't worry! We'll order milk!

18:46.560 --> 18:51.210
Man, kids these days have expensive tastes.

18:53.270 --> 18:55.230
<b><i>Any recognizable traits?</i></b>

18:53.270 --> 18:55.230
<b><i>I think I found people involved
 in the human knot case.

 Traits: 
 Sailor suit 
 Glasses 
 Braided hair 
 Highlights on bangs 
 Platform pumps 
 Knee socks 
 Red choker 
 Teen girl</i></b>

19:01.160 --> 19:03.420
Hey, you two.

19:03.910 --> 19:10.230
If I treat you to some juice, will you 
tell me what kids these days are into?

19:12.330 --> 19:13.000
Huh?

19:13.830 --> 19:14.750
Arase.

19:15.060 --> 19:16.300
Where's he—

19:16.300 --> 19:17.850
Wait, he's headed toward...

19:18.210 --> 19:18.920
No way!

19:18.210 --> 19:18.920
<b>12 minutes</b>

19:18.920 --> 19:19.850
Hot!

19:20.210 --> 19:21.970
I spilled it!

19:22.620 --> 19:24.720
That was a close one.

19:24.720 --> 19:27.770
So then Hagane-chan said,

19:27.770 --> 19:30.130
"Damn your impudence!"

19:30.740 --> 19:32.850
That's something cannon fodder would say!

19:32.850 --> 19:35.320
Who's Hagane-chan, anyway?

19:35.570 --> 19:39.280
<i>What is this fruit juice?</i>

19:39.540 --> 19:45.210
<i>It's more delicious than any drink 
I tasted before I became undead!</i>

19:46.570 --> 19:49.770
<i>I wish I could have shared it with 
everyone in the abandoned coal mine.</i>

19:50.210 --> 19:51.990
What's he crying for?

19:51.990 --> 19:53.210
Beats me.

19:53.490 --> 19:55.750
<i>Hey, Polka! Are you in the bar?!</i>

19:55.750 --> 19:57.100
<i>Don't answer!</i>

19:57.100 --> 19:59.800
<i>If you're there, go out the back door ASAP!</i>

20:04.120 --> 20:07.300
Would you let me past? I'm a customer.

20:07.820 --> 20:10.680
At least for now.

20:12.060 --> 20:14.070
It's all right. Let him in.

20:14.520 --> 20:16.530
His friend is already here.

20:16.530 --> 20:19.070
Yo, Arase! Over here!

20:19.070 --> 20:20.360
She-fox.

20:21.780 --> 20:24.500
I never thought I'd actually 
find you with them.

20:24.980 --> 20:25.870
Hey!

20:25.870 --> 20:29.270
That's the bad guy who tried 
to hit me and force himself on me!

20:29.270 --> 20:30.010
Huh?

20:30.010 --> 20:32.220
I did <i>not</i> try to force myself on you.

20:32.220 --> 20:34.330
Yuck! How scummy can you be?

20:34.330 --> 20:35.980
Inspector?

20:35.980 --> 20:38.060
I'm just kidding.

20:38.670 --> 20:43.140
Listen, do you mind if I 
ask you some questions?

20:43.630 --> 20:48.220
You don't wanna get charged with 
obstruction of justice, do you?

20:51.450 --> 20:53.370
Damn! I've had it with your tricks!

20:53.370 --> 20:54.830
That wasn't us.

20:55.500 --> 20:58.830
What'll we do now, Polka-kun? Run for it?

20:58.830 --> 21:00.920
That sounds like a good idea.

21:06.300 --> 21:08.510
You hold my hand this time.

21:09.930 --> 21:13.450
Wow! You come on strong.

21:23.370 --> 21:24.340
Polka-kun?

21:25.630 --> 21:28.800
<i>What is it? What's in here?!</i>

21:29.290 --> 21:31.010
I'm going to make some light.

21:54.540 --> 21:57.130
You've gotta be kidding me.

21:59.370 --> 22:01.040
What's <i>he</i> doing here?

22:01.790 --> 22:03.270
Lemmings!
